  "notes": "The cast and trigger rules of planeswalker-party-guff.json (its notes say why each exists) without the go-wide attack: Forge declares the attacks. Why it exists: the go-wide policy sends every creature that can attack, which here means the Wizards that pay for planeswalkers, the tokens that would block for them and planeswalkers that Sarkhan or Sparkshaper Visionary turned into creatures; against three opponents that do nothing this is free, at a table it may not be, and goldfish cannot say. Goldfish on the 40 validation seeds (2701-2740): 11.32 turns against stock's 13.07, 1.75 faster (95% +0.89 to +2.61; faster in 26, the same in 9, slower in 5), and 0.68 slower than the go-wide file (95% 0.44 to 0.91). Played after the rules had been changed once on these seeds (the hold on Chandra, Legacy of Fire's 0 under 40 cards, added because this arm lost seed 2707 to an empty library without it; the other 39 games are the same with and without the hold). Not played at tables.",
